  "overview": {
    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Herb W. Morgan is a retired investment executive. He served as board chair of the San Diego City Employees' Retirement System. He founded an investment firm in San Diego that was later acquired by Cantor Fitzgerald Investment Advisors.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Herb W. Morgan is a retired investment executive.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He served as board chair of the San Diego City Employees' Retirement System.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "He founded an investment firm in San Diego that was later acquired by Cantor Fitzgerald Investment Advisors.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He campaigns on a platform he calls Radical Transparency, and proposes publishing all state spending on a public, real-time blockchain ledger and using artificial intelligence to audit for fraud. He wants to automatically withhold funds from programs that fail audits and require zero-based budgeting. He would prioritize audits of non-governmental organizations that receive state homelessness money. He opposes raising the minimum wage, arguing government mandates raise costs and kill jobs. He opposes a \"split roll\" revision to Proposition 13, saying it would harm California’s business climate. His campaign says the state’s budget masks a roughly $20 billion structural deficit.",
        "cites": [4, 5, 6, 7]
      },
      {
        "text": "His campaign says he collaborated with other trustees to overhaul the retirement system's financial reporting and governance. He built a transparency platform, California Radical Transparency, that his campaign says analyzed over 122 million state financial records covering nearly $2 trillion in transactions. His campaign’s white paper estimated $312 billion to $425 billion in potential waste, fraud, and improper payments over five years.",
        "cites": [2, 8, 9],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "His campaign says he collaborated with other trustees to overhaul the retirement system's financial reporting and governance.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "He built a transparency platform, California Radical Transparency, that his campaign says analyzed over 122 million state financial records covering nearly $2 trillion in transactions.",
            "cites": [8]
          },
          {
            "text": "His campaign’s white paper estimated $312 billion to $425 billion in potential waste, fraud, and improper payments over five years.",
            "cites": [9]
          }
        ]
      }
